# Code owners for the release surface.
#
# This gates contributors, not the release manager: @Decipher is listed in the
# branch's bypass_pull_request_allowances, so a release manager's own pull
# request needs no second approval. It takes effect once
# require_code_owner_reviews is enabled on the release lines.
#
# Keep these paths narrow. Owning packages/*/package.json would put the gate on
# every dependency bump, which is not the intent.

# The release decision. A changelog is generated by `changeset version`, so in
# practice the version pull request is the only thing that edits one.
packages/*/CHANGELOG.md        @Decipher
RELEASING.md                   @Decipher

# The gate itself, so it cannot be relaxed in the change it gates.
.github/CODEOWNERS             @Decipher
.github/workflows/release.yml  @Decipher
scripts/release/               @Decipher
